{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1511320-1e-homebrew-the-court-of-birth","id":1511320,"title":"1e Homebrew - the Court of Birth","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-10T20:00:06-07:00","id":1511320,"title":"1e Homebrew - the Court of Birth","content":"<span style=\"font-size:22px\">The Court of Birth.</span><br /> <b>(The Alabaster Court, the Nursery, the Court of Curiosity)</b>\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>We never stop </i>being<i>, have you never noticed that? No matter how twisted we got. No matter how many times we die and are born again some essential part remains. Would you like to know what it is?</i><br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>T</b>he Court of Birth is the one changelings flock to when they feel a need for new beginnings. Some of the higher members of the Court would argue that life, no matter whose living it is, is made of a series of endings followed by beginnings.<br /> <br /> The Lost of this court support each other through many kinds of ventures, given that their chosen emotion is Curiosity they are always ready to die and be brought back by the satisfaction that follows.<br /> <br /> One might argue sticking your nose where it doesn't belong all the time is a surefire way to get recaptured, the Nursery doesn't see it that way. To them, birth is the lynchpin of growth; to grow is to change, and to change is to live.<br /> <br /> <b>Courtiers</b><br /> <br /> The Court of Curiosity makes it hard for changelings to be accepted but they also make it seem easy. They scout new potential members, and take care of them, and when they feel one is a potential candidate they entice one's Curiosity, and if a candidate follows the breadcrumb and solves the puzzle he's in. Actually solving the puzzle though, is less important than the will to never give up<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Rituals</b><br /> This is one of the most varied courts when it comes to rituals. Several religions and philosophies are celebrated.<br /> Special mention should be given to certain pagan midsummer festivals, reading of Jewish and Christian holy books, and heated discussion in greek chambers..<br /> <br /> <b>Heraldry</b><br /> The court's colors are white gold and blue, its symbols are adorned weapons as well as all kinds of white feathered birds<br /> symbolizing birth and rebirth.<br /> <br /> <b>Curiosity.</b><br /> <br /> The court's chosen emotion of curiosity is the beginning of all learning, those who lack curiosity never truly gain new knowledge and thus become stagnant. That's Curiosity's main use, a bulwark against stagnance.<br /> \u200bMantle<br /> <br /> The Birth Court's Mantle put those who wear it at the center of attention, which mantle \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022 they emit a soft pulsing golden-white white that is pleasant to the eye, a chorus of birdsong as well as the smell of Frankincense might be around the Mantle's Wearer<br /> At Mantle \u2022+ the Changeling may gain a Speciality in her Investigation Skill<br /> When she teaches Mable \u2022\u2022\u2022+ she gains a +2 bonus on any Subterfuge rolls to sneak around in and out of place<br /> At Mantle \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 she suffers no Untrained Penalties on any skills.<br /> <br /> <b>The Contract of Birth.</b><br /> <br /> (\u2022) Cost:<br /> Dice Pool:<br /> Action:<br /> Catch:.<br /> Roll Results<br /> Dramatic Failure:<br /> Failure: Success:<br /> Exceptional Success:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Birth Answer(\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> The Changeling may literally create,on his mind,the answer to a riddle,conundrum,equation and the like<br /> <br /> Cost: 1 Glamour<br /> <br /> Dice Pool: Wits + Wyrd<br /> <br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> Catch: The Changeling ia dressed like a scholar<br /> <br /> Roll Results<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The Changeling creates the wrong answer.<br /> <br /> Failure: Success: the energies of the wyrd simply fail to work<br /> <br /> Success: the Changeling suddenly knows the answer to a difficult question. The question has to be something discoverable by mundane means, even if it's extremely hard mundane means. Such as the password of a president's bank account<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: the Changeling may use the contract a second time In the same scene<br /> <br /> <b>Birth Tool (\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Cost: 2 Glamour<br /> <br /> Dice Pool: Crafts + Wyrd<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Catch: The Changeling is dressed like a craftsman<br /> <br /> The canny fae always has the right tool for the job. In a fight they have knives, in a cell they have keys<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: the contract creates a useless tool<br /> Failure: the energies of the wyrd do not answer<br /> Success: the Changeling shoves his hand into an unseen space and they come back with an appropriate tool. A knife, a key, or even a credit card with some amount of money (equivalent to resources 2)<br /> Exceptional Success: the tools are even better. Instead of a knife, you get a gun, instead of a key, you get a master key instead of a credit card with resources 2 you get one resource 4.<br /> <br /> <b>Birth Ephemera(\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Ephemera are no strangers to Changelings, but only those in possession of this contract can create them at will.<br /> <br /> Cost: 2 Glamour<br /> Dice Pool: Subterfuge + Wyrd<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Catch: the Changeling is dressed like an occultist<br /> Roll Results<br /> Dramatic Failure: the spirit is created and he absolutely hates his creator<br /> Failure: the energies of the wyrd fail to respond<br /> Success: The Changeling breathes out a spirit that he can see and interact with in the spirit frequency of twilight. The spirit is Rank 1 and it's well disposed towards the changeling<br /> Exceptional Success: not only is the spirit rank 2 but its super well disposed towards the Changeling<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Birth Hob(\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Hobgoblins are mighty useful, it's always good to have one in the pocket<br /> Cost: 3 Glamour<br /> Dice Pool: Survival + Wyrd<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Catch:.the Changeling is dressed like a wilderness explorer<br /> Roll Results<br /> Dramatic Failure: the hobgoblin is created and it hates the changeling<br /> Failure: the energies of the wyrd fail to respond<br /> Success: the Changeling creates a young hobgoblin who's loyal to her<br /> Exceptional Success: the hobgoblin is stronger and is even more loyal to the changeling<br /> <br /> <b>Birth Hollow(\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> There's always a safe for those who know to find or create them<br /> <br /> Cost: 3 Glamour<br /> Dice Pool: Survival + Craft<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Catch: The Changeling is dressed like an architect<br /> Roll Results<br /> Dramatic Failure: the hedge around the Changeling becomes hostile<br /> Failure: the energies of the wyrd fail to respond<br /> Success: the Changeling creates a rank 5 Hollow which last until the next sunrise<br /> Exceptional Success: The Hollow lasts thirteen days.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}